& [IR6CoordinationBoundaryImportAndInvariantReconciliationV1] is the IR6-S01 boundary map for coordination mailbox and claim projection prototype planning
  + [boundary_map_id] is ir6-coordination-boundary-import-and-invariant-reconciliation-v1
  + [boundary_map_uuid] is 96e051f8-8ecb-4947-ad72-9c00928ab1d2
  + [slice_id] is IR6-S01
  + [source_chunk] is IR6 coordination mailbox and claim projection prototype
  + [authority_scope] is imported coordination contracts, imported surface projection contracts, imported operations safety contracts, imported IR5 implementation proof, claim authority ladder, mailbox carrier non-authority boundary, identity preservation rules, stale triggers, and forbidden mutation boundaries
  + [implementation_scope] is boundary import and invariant reconciliation only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: import accepted coordination, surface, operations, and IR5 proof boundaries before defining claim identity, mailbox carrier, conflict review, fixture, or implementation contracts
  = must: preserve coordination claims as work-boundary records, not source authority, dispatch authority, completion authority, or live-control authority
  = must: preserve rendezvous packets, mailbox messages, IRC logs, Matrix events, web events, terminal output, Codex state, Langflow diagrams, and generated projections as carrier or projection context only
  = must: preserve conversation identity, claimant identity, claim basis, file and artifact scope, release context, and conflict lineage before any downstream projection suggests action
  = must: preserve dry-run-only operations semantics and live-control refusal when coordination requests resemble dispatch, process control, job control, GPU control, or machine-control authority
  - never: implement executable coordination code, mailbox transport, chat adapters, claim storage, fixture files, expected ledgers, generated output writers, dependency installation, operations simulator code, agent dispatch, operations control, or live machine control in this slice

