& [ReconciledIR6InvariantSet] is the reconciled invariant set for IR6 coordination mailbox and claim projection prototype planning
  + [invariant] is SOP source documents, accepted canonical specifications, accepted packs, accepted proofs, accepted completion reviews, accepted human override records, and SJS-signed artifacts remain source authority
  + [invariant] is coordination claims coordinate work boundaries only and never validate source specifications, accept completed work, assign agents, dispatch jobs, authorize dependencies, or authorize operations control
  + [invariant] is every coordination claim must preserve claimant_ref, conversation_ref, work_packet_ref, scope_subject_ref, file_scope_set, artifact_scope_set, intended_output_set, authority_basis_ref_set, claim_state, freshness_rule, conflict_policy, and release_condition
  + [invariant] is proposed, active, contested, stale, released, superseded, and invalidated claims remain visible as lineage rather than being deleted or merged silently
  + [invariant] is incompatible active write claims cannot both be projected as current and must emit contested claim or SOP-first interrupt context before follow-on work proceeds
  + [invariant] is compatible parallel claims require explicit non-overlap or read-only classification and must preserve separate conversation identities
  + [invariant] is stale claims block readiness only until review can classify refresh, release, supersession, invalidation, or rebake route
  + [invariant] is rendezvous packets and mailbox messages carry durable context but are not signed authority by themselves
  + [invariant] is mailbox read cursors and inbox timestamps are freshness evidence only and cannot erase unread context, source authority, or claim lineage
  + [invariant] is inbound claim, release, conflict, review, human override, or mailbox action requests from any carrier must be classified before an authority-sensitive route can run
  + [invariant] is ambiguous identity, missing claimant, missing conversation, hidden scope expansion, stale basis, unsupported scope, authority conflict, contested claim, or human override requirement routes to SOP-first interrupt, coordination review, completion review, or rebake rather than silent mutation
  + [invariant] is IR5 surface projections may display coordination state only as authority-noticed projection evidence over accepted records and cannot open gates directly
  + [invariant] is operation-like or dispatch-like coordination requests are operation request records, refusal records, dry-run planning records, or safety review requests only
  + [invariant] is broad approval, projected user intent, mailbox notice, active claim, dry-run success, fixture success, or carrier state cannot authorize live control
  + [invariant] is generated-output roots, fixture roots, expected ledgers, mailbox carrier paths, adapter queues, and surface caches stay outside source authority unless a later accepted slice explicitly defines a bounded generated-output policy

  = must: preserve these invariants through IR6-S02 through IR6-S07
  = must: route invariant contradictions through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

& [CoordinationAuthorityLadder: IR6] is the authority ladder that all downstream IR6 projections must preserve
  + [authority_tier] is source_authority
  + [source_authority_member] is preserved source specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted canonical specification
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted SJS satisfaction signature
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted proof pack
  + [source_authority_member] is accepted completion review
  + [source_authority_member] is explicit accepted human override record with authority notice
  + [authority_tier] is coordination_boundary_record
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is accepted work_packet
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is active coordination_claim
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is contested coordination_claim
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is stale coordination_claim
  + [coordination_boundary_record_member] is release, supersession, or invalidation notice accepted by reviewable route
  + [authority_tier] is accepted_execution_evidence
  + [accepted_execution_evidence_member] is operator_trace accepted through proof or completion review
  + [accepted_execution_evidence_member] is coordination_conflict_signal accepted through proof or completion review
  + [authority_tier] is generated_projection_evidence
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated coordination projection
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated mailbox projection
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is generated report
  + [generated_projection_evidence_member] is fixture output
  + [authority_tier] is carrier_context
  + [carrier_context_member] is mailbox file path
  + [carrier_context_member] is inbox timestamp
  + [carrier_context_member] is read cursor
  + [carrier_context_member] is chat message
  + [carrier_context_member] is Codex thread state
  + [carrier_context_member] is terminal output
  + [carrier_context_member] is IRC log
  + [carrier_context_member] is Matrix event
  + [carrier_context_member] is web request state
  + [carrier_context_member] is Langflow diagram

  = must: display lower authority tier and trust limit anywhere lower-tier records may influence action
  = must: prevent lower tiers from satisfying source-authority obligations without accepted promotion through proof, SJS, human override, or completion review

& [ClaimAndMailboxBoundaryImportMap: IR6] is the imported coordination contract map for downstream IR6 projection work
  + [projection_family] is claim identity projection imports CoordinationClaimLifecycle, CoordinationClaimBoundary, StaleClaimRuleSet, MultiAgentWorkBoundaryInvariant, AuthorityNoticeContract, and FalseReadyPreventionRule
  + [projection_family] is claim conflict projection imports coordination_conflict_signal, contested claim blocker, hidden scope expansion fault, ambiguous identity interrupt, stale claim refresh route, and completion review gate
  + [projection_family] is rendezvous packet projection imports RendezvousPacketContract, authority_notice, requested_response, stale_after, source_ref_set, lineage_edge_set, and carrier-only transport policy
  + [projection_family] is mailbox projection imports mailbox file path, inbox timestamp, read cursor, unread notice set, addressed_to_ref, sender_ref, conversation_ref, related_work_packet_ref, related_coordination_claim_ref, and carrier-only status
  + [projection_family] is manager coordination projection imports ManagerProjectionContract, ClaimVisibilityRule, SupportRequirementDeltaVisibilityRule, current_ready_slice_or_chunk, contested_claim_set, pending_review_set, and supported_action_route_set
  + [projection_family] is narrative reentry projection imports CompactionReentryProjectionRule, rendezvous_packet_ref_set, coordination_claim_ref_set, unresolved frontier set, stale trigger set, and conversation identity preservation
  + [projection_family] is conversation adapter projection imports InboundActionClassificationRule, AdapterMutationThroughOperatorGate, MultiSurfaceDivergenceRule, and CarrierContextRule
  + [projection_family] is operations safety projection imports machine-control non-authority and live-control prohibition for dispatch-like or operation-like coordination requests

  = must: require IR6-S02 to define claim identity and work-boundary projection before mailbox carrier contracts, fixtures, implementation activation plans, or generated outputs are created
  = must: refuse any projection family that cannot preserve authority notice, freshness, lineage, claim state, identity separation, and stop-state visibility

& [IR5SurfaceProjectionProofHandoffForIR6] is the handoff from accepted IR5 surface projection implementation proof into IR6 coordination planning
  + [handoff_source] is IR5SurfaceProjectionPrototypeImplementationProofPackV1
  + [usable_evidence] is authority display model preserving authority notice, lineage, freshness, and stop-state visibility
  + [usable_evidence] is projection state model preserving projected status, invalidation references, blocked items, contested claims, fault items, and pending reviews
  + [usable_evidence] is action route classifier refusing direct mutation, direct completion acceptance, live control, and direct claim acceptance
  + [usable_evidence] is fixture runner proof that generated outputs remain disposable and non-authoritative
  + [handoff_limit] is IR5 projection proof may inform coordination projection state but may not become claim authority, mailbox authority, dispatch authority, operation authority, or live-control authority

  = must: show IR5-derived projection state as projection evidence unless accepted by completion review
  = must: fault or interrupt any future coordination surface that treats projection state as claim, source, dispatch, or mailbox authority

& [OperationsSafetyHandoffForIR6] is the handoff from accepted FSC5 operations safety into IR6 coordination planning
  + [handoff_source] is FSC5OperationsSafetyPackV1
  + [usable_evidence] is operation request schema
  + [usable_evidence] is intended effect classification
  + [usable_evidence] is resource target classification
  + [usable_evidence] is refusal output contract
  + [usable_evidence] is machine-control non-authority rule
  + [usable_evidence] is live-control prohibition gate
  + [handoff_limit] is coordination surfaces may display or request dry-run planning records only; no command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, operations control, or live machine control is authorized

  = must: convert dispatch-like or operation-like coordination requests into classified requests, refusal records, or SOP-first interrupt contexts
  = must: keep human approval display separate from live-control permission until a separate future live-control authority is source-preserved, SJS-processed, and accepted

& [IR6GeneratedOutputAndFixtureBoundary] is the generated-output and fixture boundary for IR6-S01
  + [fixture_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_ledger_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_projection_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [mailbox_transport_output_creation_authorized] is false
  + [future_fixture_slice] is IR6-S05 after IR6-S01 through IR6-S04 acceptance
  + [future_generated_output_policy_slice] is IR6-S06 after IR6-S05 acceptance
  + [current_generated_output_role] is none_created_by_this_slice
  + [future_generated_output_default_authority] is non_authoritative_projection_only

  = must: reject IR6-S01 completion if fixture sources, expected ledgers, generated output files, mailbox files, adapter queues, carrier caches, or projection reports are created
  = must: require later accepted generated-output policy before any generated coordination projection root can be trusted even as disposable evidence

& [ForbiddenIR6S01MutationList] is the forbidden mutation set for IR6-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted FSC2, FSC4, FSC5, IR5, or IR6 authority inputs to make reconciliation easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating coordination claims as source authority, dispatch authority, completion authority, or operations authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating rendezvous packets or mailbox messages as signed authority by themselves
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating carrier context as a claim state transition without accepted coordination operator or completion review evidence
  + [forbidden_mutation] is collapsing claimant identity, conversation identity, or work-packet identity across participants
  + [forbidden_mutation] is hiding contested claims, stale claims, ambiguous identities, hidden scope expansion, human override context, or pending review state
  + [forbidden_mutation] is resolving incompatible claims silently
  + [forbidden_mutation] is deleting stale, released, superseded, or invalidated claim lineage
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing mailbox transport, IRC, Matrix, web, terminal, Codex, Langflow, or chat adapter behavior
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing dependencies or mutating package metadata
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating fixture source files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating expected ledger files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating generated output files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing operations simulator code
  + [forbidden_mutation] is dispatching agents, jobs, commands, processes, GPU work, model runtimes, or persistent operations automation
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control or live machine control

  = must: fail IR6-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR6] is the stale trigger set for downstream IR6 work
  + [stale_trigger] is IR6 canonical specification hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR6 final slice surface changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR6 minting review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC2 planning coordination pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is coordination claim and rendezvous contract hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC4 surface projection pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is FSC5 operations safety pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR5 implementation proof pack hash changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR5 implementation completion review changes
  + [stale_trigger] is IR5 work state changes
  + [stale_trigger] is authority notice contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is manager, worker, narrative, debug, conversation, or adapter projection contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is operations safety or live-control prohibition contract changes
  + [stale_trigger] is missing authority_notice detected in downstream coordination display contract
  + [stale_trigger] is hidden contested claim, stale claim, ambiguous identity, hidden scope expansion, interrupted path, faulted path, or pending-review state detected
  + [stale_trigger] is generated projection, carrier context, mailbox path, inbox timestamp, read cursor, dry-run, fixture result, or human approval display treated as source authority
  + [stale_trigger] is operation-like projection or coordination request treated as permission for dispatch, command execution, or live-control effect

  = must: mark affected downstream slices stale when any listed trigger fires
  = must: route stale-trigger repair through completion review and rebake rather than silent edits

